{"name":"Harvard Crimson","hex":"#c90016","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"crimson","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A deep, slightly bluish red."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a deep red colour.","Immodest. (Can we add an example for this sense?)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crimson"}],"entries":[{"title":"Harvard Crimson","blocks":[{"text":"The Harvard Crimson is the nickname of the college sports teams of Harvard University. The school's teams compete in NCAA Division I. As of 2013, there were 42 Division I intercollegiate varsity sports teams for women and men at Harvard, more than at any other NCAA Division I college in the country. Like the other Ivy League colleges, Harvard does not offer athletic scholarships."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Harvard_Crimson_logo_2020.svg/330px-Harvard_Crimson_logo_2020.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harvard_Crimson","wikidata":"Q1573151"},{"title":"Harvard University","blocks":[{"text":"Harvard University is a private Ivy League research university in Cambridge, Massachusetts, United States. Founded in 1636, and named Harvard College in 1639 in honor of its first benefactor, Puritan clergyman John Harvard, it is the oldest institution of higher learning in the United States. Its influence, wealth, and rankings have made it one of the most prestigious universities in the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Harvard_University_coat_of_arms.svg/330px-Harvard_University_coat_of_arms.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harvard_University","wikidata":"Q13371"},{"title":"Crimson","blocks":[{"text":"Crimson is a rich, deep red color, inclining to purple. It originally meant the color of the kermes dye produced from a scale insect, Kermes vermilio, but the name is now sometimes also used as a generic term for slightly bluish-red colors that are between red and rose. It is the national color of Nepal."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Maple_Leaf_Red_Ground_2000px.jpg/330px-Maple_Leaf_Red_Ground_2000px.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crimson","wikidata":"Q303826"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Harvard_crimsons_v_brown_2009.JPG/500px-Harvard_crimsons_v_brown_2009.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Harvard_crimsons_v_brown_2009.JPG/1280px-Harvard_crimsons_v_brown_2009.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Harvard_crimsons_v_brown_2009.JPG/500px-Harvard_crimsons_v_brown_2009.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Harvard football taking on Brown at Harvard Stadium in September 2009","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHarvard_crimsons_v_brown_2009.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Harvard_Crimson_players_after_game.jpg/500px-Harvard_Crimson_players_after_game.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Harvard_Crimson_players_after_game.jpg/1280px-Harvard_Crimson_players_after_game.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Harvard_Crimson_players_after_game.jpg/500px-Harvard_Crimson_players_after_game.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Harvard men's ice hockey team in 2023","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/